faqs:
  - q: "Can HubSpot lifecycle stages move backwards?"
    a: "Not by default. HubSpot is designed to move lifecycle stages forward, so a workflow or import will not set an earlier stage on its own. To move a record back, for example a closed-lost opportunity returning to lead, clear the lifecycle stage property first and then set the earlier value, and document when that is allowed."
  - q: "What is the difference between an MQL and an SQL?"
    a: "A marketing qualified lead has shown enough fit and engagement for marketing to hand it over. A sales qualified lead has been reviewed by sales and accepted as worth active pursuit. The exact criteria are yours to define, and both teams should sign them off in writing."
  - q: "Should every contact have a lifecycle stage?"
    a: "Yes. A blank lifecycle stage makes funnel reports incomplete and routing unpredictable. Set a default on every entry point, such as forms, imports, and integrations, so new records always start in a known stage."
  - q: "How do lifecycle stages relate to deal stages?"
    a: "Lifecycle stage describes the contact or company relationship; deal stage describes one specific opportunity in a pipeline. A company can be a customer with a new deal open. Many teams move records to opportunity when a deal is created and to customer when a deal is closed won."
